TinyUSB vendored sources — trimmed copy for the Arduino Renesas RA4M1 core
(Uno R4 Minima / Nano R4). Installed into the core by
scripts/patch_renesas_core.{sh,macos.sh,windows.ps1}, which copies every entry
except PIN, SHA256SUMS and VERSION.

Upstream: https://github.com/hathach/tinyusb
Ref:      master
Commit:   e20482387575da72b11d84ed008b25a28e068a01
Date:     2026-10-08
Subject:  rp2040/hcd: abort EPX transfers and release the buffer of a failed one (#4166)

TRIMMED: device + host stacks and every class driver the R4 can host or
expose. Kept: audio (device+host), cdc (+ serial ftdi_sio/cp210x/pl2303/ch34x),
dfu + dfu_rt, hid, midi + midi2, msc, net (ncm/ecm_rndis), printer
(device+host), usbtmc, vendor. Dropped: bth, mtp, video, typec, and every
portable/ vendor tree except renesas/rusb2.

LOCAL DEVIATIONS FROM UPSTREAM (all bench-proven on R4 hardware)
--------------------------------------------------------------
portable/renesas/rusb2/hcd_rusb2.c
  - process_pipe0_xfer() OUT data stage: re-assert DCPCFG.DIR=1. hcd_setup_send()
    sets DIR from bmRequestType but it is cleared before the data stage runs,
    so the hardware issues an IN token mid-transfer and vendor OUT control
    transfers with data (CP2102 SET_BAUDRATE) stall. Also drops the BSTS
    assert, which fired spuriously, and inverts the USBREQ direction test.
  - process_pipe0_xfer() ZLP branch: set PID=NAK instead of asserting it.
    PID is still BUF after an OUT data stage, so the ACK stage of a control
    OUT transfer with data was never submitted (transfer hung).
  - dcd/hcd SACK ISR: set PID=NAK before handing the data stage to
    process_pipe0_xfer(). Without it the hardware can issue a token before the
    FIFO is populated, firing BRDY with stale pipe state (remaining=0).
  All three are still absent upstream.

host/usbh.c
  - usbh_control_xfer_cb(): drop completions whose endpoint does not match the
    outstanding stage. Under a backlogged event queue a stale DATA completion
    surfaces during a later EP0 transfer, and the single shared control slot
    cannot tell them apart (observed: 8B/9B ghosts consumed as the data of a
    62B RANGE read, killing audio mount).
  - PRINTER class driver table entry (backport; the driver is absent upstream).

class/printer/printer_host.{c,h}
  - Backport. The whole PRINTER host driver is absent upstream as of this
    commit; only the device side exists. Backported from TinyUSB_Arduino.

class/msc/msc_host.c
  - Per-LUN Test-Unit-Ready + Read-Capacity walk during config, bounded to
    5 Request-Sense retries (MSC_SENSE_MAX_RETRIES). Upstream probes only LUN 0
    and retries TUR unbounded, so a multi-LUN reader with an empty slot hangs
    the mount forever. max_lun is clamped to CFG_TUH_MSC_MAXLUN.
  - Mount fires once every LUN has been probed, including when none is ready,
    so hot-inserted media and an app-driven rescan still work.
  - tuh_msc_scsi_command(): reject unless the stage machine is IDLE. Issuing a
    CBW mid-flight overwrites the in-flight command's buffer/callback/stage.
  - READ_CAPACITY_10 completions refresh capacity[lun] for app-initiated reads
    too, not just the config-time probe.
  Upstream's chunked data stage (MSCH_DATA_XFER_MAX) is preserved as-is.

class/cdc/cdc_host.c
  - make_new_itf() initialises line coding to 8N1 @9600. Upstream zero-inits it,
    and the PL2303 driver silently rejects a zero data_bits, so the port never
    opens after a bare tuh_cdc_set_baudrate().

